Jacobs wrote:

> There aren't any very real restrictions on wizmode anyway.  Well, on 
> Debian apparently, but not otherwise.  Anyone who I allowed to use my 
> computer could leave bones files from wizard mode if they chose.

Sure, if you gave everyone the password for the wizard account, or if
you're running Windows (this issue isn't present in the Windows version,
AFAIK.  I will refrain, however, from starting an anti-Windows diatribe
here :) )

> I don't think the restrictions are useful now unless there are some that 
> I don't understand and I think few people share their computers with 
> cheaters and don't know it, so I don't think we really need any 
> protections.

There are good reasons to prevent this besides honesty -- people can make
mistakes, too.  This is one important reason why people running personal
unix systems with no other users still have a separate administrator (root)
account.

We also don't want to make it even easier to spoil hearse bones files,
which would probably start to happen unintentionally if all restrictions
were removed.  I had to #quit a promising game where this occurred once,
and would hate to see it become more frequent.

